  "sport": "basketball",
  "title": "Beat the one behind – line shooting game",
  "description": "All players line up behind the free-throw line. The first two in the line have a ball each. The first player shoots from the free-throw line. As soon as the ball has left their hand, the next player may shoot. If you miss, chase your own ball and try to score as quickly as you can, from anywhere. If the player behind you scores before you do, you are out.\n\nOnce you score, pass the ball to the first player in the line without a ball and go to the back of the line. The game goes on until one player is left. Players who are out can shoot free throws at a side basket instead of just waiting.\n\nVariations: move the starting spot closer for younger players, or let players who are out come back in by making three free throws in a row. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Stay calm on the first shot – a make there gives you a head start."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "If you miss: follow the ball straight away and get the rebound before it bounces off."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Close to the basket: a safe lay-up beats a rushed shot."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Pass the ball clearly to the next in line – it is part of the game."
    }
  ],
